Solar-1 monitoring, a prototype version
---------------------------------------

Fetch from NOAA and display Solar-1 proton data for the eight channels
with energies corresponding to those of the ACE proton channels.

Calculate, store, and plot Solar-1 P3 2-hour fluence.

Fetch ACE P3 from the local 7-day MTA archive and display for comparison.

Calculate and display ACE P3  2-hour fluence.

WORKFLOW
---------
- Perform the initial data fetch from NOAA (time range governed by dt_hours, 7 days
  by default)
- Save the data locally, fill in missing values with NaN (proton_history.parquet)
- With every consequtive execution (every minute), read in the history file, fetch
  data covering the last overlap_minutes (5 minutes by default), merge with the
  data from the history, remove duplicates by keeping the most recent entries.
- Save the updated history covering dt_hours to the parquet file.
- Calculate Solar-1 P3 2-hour fluence and save it in fluence_history.parquet file.
- Load ACE P3 data from the local MTA 7-day archive.
- Calculate ACE P3 2-hour fluence.
- Publish the Solar-1 data, the ACE P3 data, and Solar-1 fluence to a json file.
- The html file reads in and visualizes the data stored in the json file.
- Crontab calls the job with flock that prevents multiple instances of a process
  from running at the same time by the means of a lock file in the /tmp directory,
  and with timeout that kills the process after a certain time (here 50 seconds).
- If two-hour P3 fluence exceeds a limit, an email is sent to a specified address,
  a local file with the alert message is saved in the local directory, a json
  state file is updated with "alerted": True, and "last_alert_time". A cooldown
  time for additional alerts is 24 hours. After this time, the P3 fluence alert
  is rearmed ("alerted": False), the local file with the alert message is removed.

SETUP
----------

Place solar1.py and fluence.py in SPACE_WEATHER=/data/mta4/Space_Weather/Solar-1
Place solar1.html in SPACE_WEATHER_WEB=/data/mta4/www/Solar-1

If proton_history.parquet and fluence_history.parquet files are available,
place them in the directory of the *.py files. Otherwise, the history files
will be created from scratch.

MTA cronjob:

* * * * * /usr/bin/flock -n /tmp/solar1.lock /usr/bin/timeout 50s ${ENV_FLIGHT}/bin/skare python ${SPACE_WEATHER}/Solar-1/solar1.py >> ${HOME}/Logs/solar1_log.cron 2>&1
* * * * * /usr/bin/flock -n /tmp/solar1_alert.lock /usr/bin/timeout 50s ${ENV_FLIGHT}/bin/skare python ${SPACE_WEATHER}/Solar-1/solar1_alert.py >> ${HOME}/Logs/solar1_alert_log.cron 2>&1

OUTPUT
------
The following file(s) will appear (or will be updated) in SPACE_WEATHER/Solar-1:
- proton_history.parquet
- fluence_history.parquet
- solar1-fluence-alert-state.json
- solar1-fluence-alert-message.txt

The following file(s) will appear in SPACE_WEATHER_WEB/Solar-1:
- solar-1-protons.json

Log file(s) with execution info, warnings, and errors:
- /home/mta/Logs/solar1_log.cron
- /home/mta/Logs/solar1_alert_log.cron

Lock file(s) will be placed in /tmp (managed with flock).

View: https://cxc.harvard.edu/mta/RADIATION/Solar-1/solar1.html


ALERTS
------
Two-hour P3 fluence
Flight threshold value = 3.8 x 10^8
Test threshold value = 1.1 x 10^6
Email sent (flight): sot_yellow_alert
Email sent (testing): MS

Files created:
- solar1-fluence-alert-state.json
- solar1-fluence-alert-message.txt

